    "narrative": "The LawDog offensive core for July 7th is led by a pair of high-ceiling plays in **Taylor Ward** (66.84) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (65.48), both of whom capitalize on prime lineup positioning and soft matchups. **Taylor Ward** benefits from a massive 16% park boost and a top-of-the-order advantage, while **Geraldo Perdomo** faces a vulnerable Marquez, utilizing a 19% SP skill advantage to anchor our production. Given our focus on the scarcest category, **Daulton Varsho** (59.90) and **Tyler Freeman** (60.52) are essential starts today; both benefit from favorable pitcher deliveries that significantly boost their probability of securing an SB, providing the legs needed to maintain our competitive edge in the standings despite facing mid-tier arms.\n\nOur most difficult decision revolved around the bench, where **Dylan Beavers** (43.29) was the odd man out. While **Dylan Beavers** carries the potential for an explosive game, his limited slot at #8 in the lineup and a challenging platoon disadvantage against the lefty Boyd pushed his efficiency below the threshold of our starters. We are managing the roster carefully today, especially as we navigate the absences of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** on the IL. We remain cautious regarding **Cal Raleigh** (51.43) and **Luis Arraez** (46.87), as both are staring down elite SP skill profiles from Meyer and Miles respectively; while **Luis Arraez** gets a marginal bump from wind conditions, his low raw score relative to **Geraldo Perdomo** suggests we are playing for contact efficiency over high-upside power today. We continue to monitor the status of **Lawrence Butler** and others, ensuring that our bench reserves remain fresh for higher-leverage matchups as we protect our daily game caps.",
